    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40532" root="نكر" body-key="n">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَنْكُورٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُنْكَرٌ</span>, first signification. The pl. is
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَنَاكِيرُ</span>, [which is also a pl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُنْكَرٌ</span>,] accord. to
Sb, who mentions it because, accord. to rule, the
pl. of a sing. of this class is formed by the addition of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">و</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ن</span> for the masc., and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ا</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ت</span> for
the fem. (Abu-l-Hasan, TA.)

